@startuml
title Operational MRI scopes and dimensions - target
rectangle "Diagnostic A:\nevidence and insight" as a
rectangle "Diagnostic B:\nevidence and insight" as b
package "Operational MRI" {
  rectangle "Shared intelligence:\nrelationships and evidence" as mri
  rectangle "Intelligence scope:\nSingle diagnostic / Team system /\nMulti-team system" as scope
  rectangle "Operational dimensions:\nClarity / Performance / Leadership /\nCulture / Foundation" as dimensions
  rectangle "Flexible taxonomy:\ncategories and elements" as taxonomy
  rectangle "Insights and presentation" as output
}
a --> mri : retained evidence and insight
b --> mri : retained evidence and insight
mri --> scope : evaluate breadth
mri --> dimensions : classify subject
dimensions --> taxonomy
scope --> output
taxonomy --> output
note bottom of scope
  Single diagnostic describes breadth; its diagnostic
  generates and interprets the insight. MRI may classify,
  organise, contextualise and present it without regenerating it.
  Team and multi-team scopes consider wider relationships.
end note
note bottom of dimensions
  Scope and dimensions are independent axes.
  An insight may have multiple associations and
  an optional primary dimension; not five engines.
end note
note bottom of mri
  Support, challenge and context are evaluated;
  another diagnostic is not automatic confirmation.
end note
@enduml
